les, which is crucial for identifying rare four tops events.\n   - The preprocessing recognizes the physics-based structure of the data with objects and their properties.\n   - The model architecture is designed to handle the sparse nature of collision data.\n\nThe solution achieves high AUC by focusing on the following key aspects:\n\n1. Effective preprocessing that preserves meaningful physical information while normalizing features.\n2. A model architecture that can capture complex relationships between particles.\n3. Robust training with regularization techniques to prevent overfitting.\n4. Direct optimization for the AUC metric by using the validation AUC for model selection and learning rate scheduling.\n\nThis approach leverages both physics knowledge and modern deep learning techniques to create an effective classifier for the four tops physics process."
